      "id": 123200,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-12-14T13:54:51.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>For your very first match I would suggest a 1v1 with characters like Wraith, Bunker, Ra, and Omnitron-V. &nbsp;Use Megalopolis, and get things like Line of Sight, Turn order, and how Aim/Dodge/Attack and Defense tokens work.</p><p>Note that the game isn't balanced for 1v1, but keeping it simple while you learn the basics of the game is a good idea.</p><p>From there move on to a bigger skirmish, 2v2 skirmishes are much more balanced, 3v3 are the best; or try a scenario.</p><p>Scenarios are almost never a straight up fight and involve different strategies than skirmishes, they are more objective based than fight based.</p><p>Baron Blade and Omnitron Scenarios are great once you have a pretty good idea what you are doing.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:57:03.809Z",
